Note: EPL HTTP Package — Make API calls in plain English
Note: Import "epl-http" to use these functions.

Note: ===========================================================
Note:  Basic HTTP Methods
Note: ===========================================================

Define Function http_get Takes url
    Note: Send a GET request and return the response
    Note: Example: Set response to http_get("https://api.example.com/users")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "get", url)
End

Define Function http_post Takes url, data
    Note: Send a POST request with JSON data
    Note: Example: Set response to http_post("https://api.example.com/users", user_data)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "post", url, data)
End

Define Function http_put Takes url, data
    Note: Send a PUT request to update a resource
    Note: Example: Set response to http_put("https://api.example.com/users/1", updated_data)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "put", url, data)
End

Define Function http_patch Takes url, data
    Note: Send a PATCH request for partial update
    Note: Example: Set response to http_patch("https://api.example.com/users/1", partial_data)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "patch", url, data)
End

Define Function http_delete Takes url
    Note: Send a DELETE request to remove a resource
    Note: Example: Set response to http_delete("https://api.example.com/users/1")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "delete", url)
End

Note: ===========================================================
Note:  Requests with Headers & Auth
Note: ===========================================================

Define Function http_get_with_headers Takes url, headers
    Note: Send a GET request with custom headers
    Note: Example: Set response to http_get_with_headers(url, {"Authorization": "Bearer token123"})
    Return python_call("epl_http", "get_with_headers", url, headers)
End

Define Function http_post_with_headers Takes url, data, headers
    Note: Send a POST request with custom headers
    Note: Example: Set response to http_post_with_headers(url, data, {"Content-Type": "application/json"})
    Return python_call("epl_http", "post_with_headers", url, data, headers)
End

Define Function http_request Takes method, url, data, headers, timeout
    Note: Send a fully customizable HTTP request
    Note: Example: Set response to http_request("POST", url, body, headers, 30)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "request", method, url, data, headers, timeout)
End

Define Function http_with_bearer_token Takes url, token
    Note: Send a GET request with Bearer token authentication
    Note: Example: Set response to http_with_bearer_token(url, "my-api-token")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "get_with_bearer", url, token)
End

Define Function http_with_basic_auth Takes url, username, password
    Note: Send a GET request with Basic authentication
    Note: Example: Set response to http_with_basic_auth(url, "admin", "secret")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "get_with_basic_auth", url, username, password)
End

Note: ===========================================================
Note:  Response Handling
Note: ===========================================================

Define Function response_status Takes response
    Note: Get the HTTP status code from a response
    Note: Example: Set code to response_status(response)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "status_code", response)
End

Define Function response_json Takes response
    Note: Parse response body as JSON
    Note: Example: Set data to response_json(response)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "json", response)
End

Define Function response_text Takes response
    Note: Get response body as plain text
    Note: Example: Set body to response_text(response)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "get_text", response)
End

Define Function response_headers Takes response
    Note: Get response headers as a dictionary
    Note: Example: Set headers to response_headers(response)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "headers", response)
End

Define Function response_is_ok Takes response
    Note: Check if the response was successful (status 200-299)
    Note: Example: If response_is_ok(response) then Say "Success!"
    Return python_call("epl_http", "is_ok", response)
End

Note: ===========================================================
Note:  JSON Utilities
Note: ===========================================================

Define Function to_json Takes data
    Note: Convert a dictionary or list to a JSON string
    Note: Example: Set json_string to to_json(my_data)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "to_json", data)
End

Define Function from_json Takes input_text
    Note: Parse a JSON string into a dictionary or list
    Note: Example: Set data to from_json(json_string)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "from_json", input_text)
End

Note: ===========================================================
Note:  File Upload & Download
Note: ===========================================================

Define Function download_file Takes url, save_path
    Note: Download a file from a URL and save it
    Note: Example: download_file("https://example.com/file.pdf", "downloads/file.pdf")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "download", url, save_path)
End

Define Function upload_file Takes url, file_path, field_name
    Note: Upload a file to a URL via multipart form
    Note: Example: upload_file("https://api.example.com/upload", "photo.jpg", "image")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "upload", url, file_path, field_name)
End

Note: ===========================================================
Note:  Webhook & Polling
Note: ===========================================================

Define Function send_webhook Takes url, event_name, payload
    Note: Send a webhook notification with event data
    Note: Example: send_webhook("https://hooks.example.com/notify", "order_placed", order_data)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "send_webhook", url, event_name, payload)
End

Define Function poll_url Takes url, interval_seconds, max_attempts
    Note: Poll a URL at intervals until success or max attempts
    Note: Example: Set result to poll_url("https://api.example.com/status", 5, 10)
    Return python_call("epl_http", "poll", url, interval_seconds, max_attempts)
End

Note: ===========================================================
Note:  URL Utilities
Note: ===========================================================

Define Function build_url Takes base, path, params
    Note: Build a URL with path and query parameters
    Note: Example: Set url to build_url("https://api.example.com", "/search", {"q": "epl"})
    Return python_call("epl_http", "build_url", base, path, params)
End

Define Function encode_url Takes input_text
    Note: URL-encode a string
    Note: Example: Set encoded to encode_url("hello world & more")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "url_encode", input_text)
End

Define Function decode_url Takes input_text
    Note: Decode a URL-encoded string
    Note: Example: Set decoded to decode_url("hello%20world")
    Return python_call("epl_http", "url_decode", input_text)
End
